    {
      "_id": "eb5c0655fea859d6",
      "name": "Psi",
      "type": "trait",
      "img": "icons/svg/upgrade.svg",
      "system": {
        "key": "psi",
        "traitType": "positive",
        "scope": "ego",
        "level": 2,
        "cost": 20,
        "costText": "Cost: 20 CP (Level 1), 25 CP (Level 2)",
        "description": "<p>The character has been infected with the WattsMacLeod strain of the Exsurgent virus, which altered their brain structure and opened the potential for their mind to enhance their cognitive abilities and read and manipulate the biological minds of others (see Psi, p. 220). The character may purchase and learn psi sleights (p. 223). At Level 1, the character may only use psi-chi sleights. At Level 2, the character may use both psi-chi and psi-gamma sleights. Though this trait is not very expensive, gamemasters should not allow it to be abused. There are a number of negative side effects to Watts-MacLeod infection, noted under Psi Drawbacks, p. 220.</p><p><em>Source: Eclipse Phase Core Rulebook, p. 147.</em></p>"
      },
      "effects": [],
      "flags": {},
      "sort": 2000,
      "ownership": {
        "default": 0
      },
      "folder": null,
      "_key": "!actors.items!5541e669e6f0a97e.eb5c0655fea859d6"
    },
    {
      "_id": "d31f37e69aba2042",
      "name": "Ambience Sense",
      "type": "sleight",
      "img": "icons/svg/daze.svg",
      "system": {
        "key": "ambienceSense",
        "psiType": "chi",
        "activation": "passive",
        "action": "automatic",
        "range": "self",
        "duration": "constant",
        "durationUnit": "turns",
        "strainMod": 0,
        "strainPerTarget": 0,
        "strainPerAP": false,
        "skill": "",
        "damage": "",
        "harm": "damage",
        "exsurgent": false,
        "active": false,
        "remaining": 0,
        "description": "<p>This sleight provides the async with an instinctive sense about an area and any potential threats nearby. The async receives a +10 modifier to all Investigation, Perception, Scrounging, and Surprise Tests.</p><p><em>Source: Eclipse Phase Core Rulebook, p. 223.</em></p>"
      },
      "effects": [],
      "flags": {},
      "sort": 3000,
      "ownership": {
        "default": 0
      },
      "folder": null,
      "_key": "!actors.items!5541e669e6f0a97e.d31f37e69aba2042"
    },
    {
      "_id": "d96a2437b58a929b",
      "name": "Grok",
      "type": "sleight",
      "img": "icons/svg/daze.svg",
      "system": {
        "key": "grok",
        "psiType": "chi",
        "activation": "active",
        "action": "complex",
        "range": "self",
        "duration": "instant",
        "durationUnit": "turns",
        "strainMod": -1,
        "strainPerTarget": 0,
        "strainPerAP": false,
        "skill": "",
        "damage": "",
        "harm": "damage",
        "exsurgent": false,
        "active": false,
        "remaining": 0,
        "description": "<p>By using the Grok sleight, the async is able to intuitively understand how any unfamiliar object, vehicle, or device is used simply by looking at and handling it. If the character succeeds in a COG x 2 Test, they achieve a basic ability to use the object, vehicle, or device, no matter how alien or bizarre. This sleight does not provide any understanding of the principles or technologies involved—the psi user simply grasps how to make it work. If a test is called for, the psi user receives a +20 modifier to use the device (this bonus only applies to unfamiliar devices, and/or tests the character is defaulting on—it does not apply to devices the character is familiar with).</p><p><em>Source: Eclipse Phase Core Rulebook, p. 224.</em></p>"
      },
      "effects": [],
      "flags": {},
      "sort": 4000,
      "ownership": {
        "default": 0
      },
      "folder": null,
      "_key": "!actors.items!5541e669e6f0a97e.d96a2437b58a929b"
    },
    {
      "_id": "f309f04b615114cd",
      "name": "Mindlink",
      "type": "sleight",
      "img": "icons/svg/terror.svg",
      "system": {
        "key": "mindlink",
        "psiType": "gamma",
        "activation": "active",
        "action": "quick",
        "range": "touch",
        "duration": "sustained",
        "durationUnit": "turns",
        "strainMod": 0,
        "strainPerTarget": 1,
        "strainPerAP": false,
        "skill": "control",
        "damage": "",
        "harm": "damage",
        "exsurgent": false,
        "active": false,
        "remaining": 0,
        "description": "<p>Mindlink allows two-way mental communication with a target. This may be used on more than one target simultaneously, in which case the async can act as a telepathic “server,” so that everyone mindlinked with the async may also telepathically communicate with each other (via the async, however, so they overhear). Language is still a factor in mindlinked communications, but this barrier may be overcome by transmitting sounds, images, emotions, and other sensations. Mindlink requires an Opposed Test against unwilling participants.</p><p><em>Source: Eclipse Phase Core Rulebook, p. 227.</em></p>"
      },
      "effects": [],
      "flags": {},
      "sort": 5000,
      "ownership": {
        "default": 0
      },
      "folder": null,
      "_key": "!actors.items!5541e669e6f0a97e.f309f04b615114cd"
    },
    {
      "_id": "ad4f274bacce2f76",
      "name": "Onslaught",
      "type": "sleight",
      "img": "icons/svg/terror.svg",
      "system": {
        "key": "onslaught",
        "psiType": "gamma",
        "activation": "active",
        "action": "complex",
        "range": "touch",
        "duration": "temporary",
        "durationUnit": "turns",
        "strainMod": 0,
        "strainPerTarget": 0,
        "strainPerAP": false,
        "skill": "psiAssault",
        "damage": "1d10 + ceil(@wil / 10)",
        "harm": "stress",
        "exsurgent": true,
        "active": false,
        "remaining": 0,
        "description": "<p>This offensive sleight floods the target’s mind with sensory input and thought processes that are so alien and disturbing that they inflict 1d10 + (WIL ÷ 10, round up) mental stress. Increase the stress by +5 if an Excellent Success is scored.</p><p><em>Source: Eclipse Phase Core Rulebook, p. 371.</em></p>"
      },
